  "body": "From the triage of CaramelizedCUDA's 26 Windows failures (#1827, https://github.com/yetone/magpie/issues/1827#issuecomment-6127633575):\n\n- The largest group, in `internal/agent`: tests sandbox `HOME`/`USERPROFILE` but leave `APPDATA` and `LOCALAPPDATA` pointing at the real or a shared folder, so on Windows one test reads another's files. The fix belongs in the shared test isolation (testenv), not per test: every per-user base dir a Windows path resolves from is pointed into the test's temp dir.\n- Tests that make a write fail with chmod 0500 or a symlink, or expect mode 0600, which Windows doesn't honour: skip on Windows or use a Windows-meaningful failure.\n- A few have Linux paths or slow-machine timing built in.\n\nWindows CI only compiles tests, so none of this shows there (LESSONS: Windows CI only compiles the tests). Run the package on the Windows box to verify.",
  "closed_by": null,
