   "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:47:03Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-10-27T21:47:03Z",
   "body": "The cause was `testenv.SetHome`: a test that took a home of its own switched `HOME` and `USERPROFILE` only, so it kept reading the package's `%APPDATA%`/`%LOCALAPPDATA%` (and on Linux `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`/`XDG_CACHE_HOME`) — one test's files in another's, the largest group in the #1827 triage.\n\nThis branch makes one list, `userDirs`, of the folders a home settles (HOME, USERPROFILE, the four XDG folders, APPDATA, LOCALAPPDATA): `Isolate` points them into the package's temporary home as before, `SetHome` into the test's own home. `syncHome` in `internal/agent` now calls `testenv.SetHome` instead of keeping its own copy of the list, so the two helpers the triage named can't drift apart again.\n\n[fix/1841-tests-internal-agent-tests-reset](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/1841-tests-internal-agent-tests-reset), commit 917d9c5a9824e84b882b386370e6bb5c5ed52f54\n\nRun: `TestSetHomePointsEveryUserBaseDirIntoTheTestHome` (new; red with the old helper — \"the config folder .../.config is outside the test home ...\", \"APPDATA is ..., outside the test home ...\" — and green with it), `go build ./...`, `GOOS=windows go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/testenv ./internal/agent`, `go test ./internal/testenv` (16 ok), `go test ./internal/agent` (its two reds, `TestAgyShell` and `TestWSLColdPlaceOpensNothing`, are red the same way at `upstream/main` on this Linux box), and the tests that call `SetHome` in `internal/gateway` (10 ok), `internal/provider` (35 ok) and `internal/gui` (7 ok). The full gateway, provider, usage, gui and plugin suites were started and not finished in this run. Not run on a Windows box — none reachable from here, so `GOOS=windows` only compiles the tests.\n\nA fork branch, ready to review; it makes no claim on the issue's ownership.\n",
